# The host's settings in a machine of the cloud pool: /etc/acme-host/host.env,
# owned by root, mode 644. Nothing in it is a secret: where the platform
# answers and the key the host trades once come from the machine's seed,
# which the pool hands each machine as it starts, on the guest's memory-backed
# /run. The host's credential lives in its home there too, so the disk the
# pool snapshots holds neither. No database login, no model key, and no
# credential of the platform's is ever here.
ACME_HOST_MACHINE_SEED=/run/acme-machine/seed.json
ACME_HOST_HOME=/run/acme-host
ACME_HOST_MACHINE_WORKSPACE=/workspace
